WEBVTT


00:01:17.387 --> 00:01:20.754
To find something, anything...


00:01:20.924 --> 00:01:25.384
...a great truth,
or a lost pair of glasses...


00:01:25.862 --> 00:01:30.265
...you must first believe there will be
some advantage in finding it.


00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.935
I found something a long time ago...


00:01:34.103 --> 00:01:37.698
...and have held on to it
for grim death ever since.


00:01:37.874 --> 00:01:40.866
I owe my success in life to it.


00:01:41.044 --> 00:01:43.512
It put me where I am today.


00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.739
This principle:


00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.584
What you don't know won't hurt you.


00:01:54.724 --> 00:01:59.593
They called it idealism
in a book I read.


00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.659
Get the gun.
Get the gun. Get the gun.


00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:19.872
Oh, my God.


00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.769
The judge won't scare easy.


00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.268
I don't count on him scaring easy.


00:03:58.114 --> 00:04:00.480
You think it's beneath my dignity?


00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.413
Well, you're governor, they tell me.


00:04:02.585 --> 00:04:05.076
Yeah, I'm governor.


00:04:05.254 --> 00:04:08.417
The trouble with governors is they
think they gotta keep their dignity.


00:04:08.591 --> 00:04:11.287
There's nothing worth doing
a man can do to keep his dignity.


00:04:11.461 --> 00:04:12.985
Human frame ain't built that way.


00:04:14.864 --> 00:04:17.264
When I'm not governor anymore
because I'm president...


00:04:17.433 --> 00:04:19.993
...I wanna meet somebody at midnight,
I'll do that then too.


00:04:20.737 --> 00:04:23.228
Hope you leave me
to get a night's sleep.


00:04:23.406 --> 00:04:26.000
No, Jack, you going with me
because that's what you want.


00:04:26.509 --> 00:04:28.636
Yeah, you and Sugar
with me in the White House.


00:04:28.811 --> 00:04:31.644
I'll give Sugar a pistol range
right out there in the garden.


00:04:32.348 --> 00:04:35.146
Brace of Republican senators
can set up his tin cans for him.


00:04:35.318 --> 00:04:37.878
And I'm gonna appoint
a special member to Cabinet for you:


00:04:38.054 --> 00:04:41.820
Secretary to the Bedchamber
of Mr. Jack Burden.


00:04:42.825 --> 00:04:45.089
Somebody to keep them
telephone numbers straight...


00:04:45.261 --> 00:04:48.753
...and return their little pink silk articles
that get left behind.


00:04:50.533 --> 00:04:52.501
But we gotta do this first.


00:04:52.668 --> 00:04:55.762
In the middle of the night when we
could just do it in town sometime.


00:04:55.938 --> 00:04:58.839
Sometime ain't never now.


00:05:00.343 --> 00:05:02.436
Bastard.


00:05:03.479 --> 00:05:04.707
Which way up there?


00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.119
Jack, tell Sugar
how to get to the house.


00:05:10.653 --> 00:05:13.349
It's your people live down here.


00:05:30.306 --> 00:05:32.035
Suppose he don't open up?


00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.370
Make him. What I pay you for?


00:06:10.713 --> 00:06:12.613
Hey, Jack.


00:06:12.782 --> 00:06:14.750
Mr. Duffy.


00:06:15.751 --> 00:06:18.117
This is Willie Stark
from up Mason City.


00:06:18.287 --> 00:06:20.255
- County treasurer.
- Glad to meet you.


00:06:21.224 --> 00:06:23.590
- Jack Burden.
- From The Chronicle.


00:06:23.759 --> 00:06:25.249
Good to meet you, Mr. Burden.


00:06:25.428 --> 00:06:27.828
Yeah, Willie's on business
for Mason City.


00:06:27.997 --> 00:06:29.328
Bond issue them got up there.


00:06:29.499 --> 00:06:31.626
Gonna build a schoolhouse.


00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:35.532
Yeah. Me and Willie
was in school together.


00:06:35.705 --> 00:06:39.607
Oh, you was in school, Alex.
I didn't know.


00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:41.868
Not the teacher's favorite,
I don't expect.


00:06:42.044 --> 00:06:44.308
No, sir, that's true.


00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.711
Willie was, though.
Still is, ain't you, Willie?


00:06:47.884 --> 00:06:50.216
Yeah, Willie married
a schoolteacher.


00:06:51.287 --> 00:06:52.515
Well, you know...


00:06:52.688 --> 00:06:56.089
...they tell me that schoolteachers
are made with it...


00:06:56.259 --> 00:06:58.124
...in the same place as the rest.


00:06:58.794 --> 00:07:01.456
Now, is that right or not, Mr. Stark?


00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:07.860
Yeah, that's right.


00:07:10.806 --> 00:07:12.273
Slade!


00:07:12.441 --> 00:07:14.375
Beers all around.


00:07:14.544 --> 00:07:16.011
Not for me, thanks.


00:07:16.178 --> 00:07:18.942
Oh, that little schoolteacher
don't like it when you drink?


00:07:19.115 --> 00:07:21.743
Well, she don't favor it, for a fact.


00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.647
Well, beers all around.


00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:29.315
Well, I sell beer
to those who want it.


00:07:29.825 --> 00:07:32.350
I don't make nobody drink them.


00:07:33.095 --> 00:07:36.326
Well, maybe you got some
orange pop for him.


00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:37.727
That's what he wants.


00:07:39.168 --> 00:07:43.195
Yeah, I think I'd like some orange pop.
Two straws.


00:07:48.477 --> 00:07:50.775
Jack, get up Mason City.


00:07:50.947 --> 00:07:53.279
See who's this fella
who thinks he's Jesus Christ...


00:07:53.616 --> 00:07:56.278
...come down off the cross to scourge
the moneychangers...


00:07:56.452 --> 00:07:59.012
...out of that shinplaster courthouse
they got them there.


00:07:59.188 --> 00:08:01.918
I know who he is.
Fella with a Christmas tie...


00:08:02.091 --> 00:08:03.524
...pushed a school bond through.


00:08:03.993 --> 00:08:06.188
- You know him?
- Met him.


00:08:06.362 --> 00:08:08.489
Watched him drink
a bottle of orange pop once...


00:08:08.664 --> 00:08:11.827
...through two straws on account
of a wife who don't favor drinking.


00:08:12.001 --> 00:08:14.162
She favor him
staying parish treasurer?


00:08:14.337 --> 00:08:16.202
Don't you know
how things are run up there?


00:08:16.372 --> 00:08:18.636
Run up there
like they're run down here.


00:08:18.808 --> 00:08:23.711
Yeah? Well, you leave down here
and run on up there.


00:08:31.621 --> 00:08:34.647
As a commissioner, as chairman,
I guess you're in a position...


00:08:34.824 --> 00:08:37.486
...to know the situation
regarding the schoolhouse contract.


00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.888
Ain't no situation.


00:08:39.061 --> 00:08:40.892
Maybe not, but maybe so.


00:08:41.063 --> 00:08:42.826
Ain't any situation.


00:08:43.332 --> 00:08:44.594
Board took a bid offer.


00:08:44.767 --> 00:08:46.860
A.J. Moore's bid, the fella's name...


00:08:47.036 --> 00:08:49.129
...schoolhouse gets built.


00:08:49.305 --> 00:08:51.637
This Moore fella's bid,
I take it, was the lowest?


00:08:52.141 --> 00:08:53.870
Now, you lookie here.


00:08:54.043 --> 00:08:57.035
Ain't nobody tells a board
what bid to take.


00:08:57.213 --> 00:09:00.148
Anybody can come along
put in a little pissant bid.


00:09:00.316 --> 00:09:01.647
Board doesn't have to take it.


00:09:01.817 --> 00:09:03.944
Board takes somebody
who can do the work right.


00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.644
Ain't nothing done but legal.


00:09:05.821 --> 00:09:08.585
Who was it
put in the little pissant bid?


00:09:08.758 --> 00:09:11.659
- Name of Jeffers, if I recollect.
- Jeffers Construction?


00:09:11.827 --> 00:09:14.625
- Yeah.
- Well, that's a real firm, a big firm.


00:09:15.498 --> 00:09:18.592
The board picks
who can do the work right.


00:09:18.768 --> 00:09:21.293
That's all I got to say.


00:09:21.937 --> 00:09:23.165
Don't you wanna tell mama...


00:09:23.339 --> 00:09:26.137
...you wanna see yourself
shining in the table? No?


00:09:26.308 --> 00:09:29.800
All right. I wish I could have
sold some to you.


00:09:29.979 --> 00:09:32.743
Be out of your way in a second here.
And no brushes, you sure?


00:09:32.915 --> 00:09:34.212
- I'm sure.
- All right.


00:09:34.383 --> 00:09:36.874
Thank you.
Thank you for your time. Bye-bye.


00:09:37.053 --> 00:09:38.281
Mr. Stark.


00:09:40.923 --> 00:09:44.791
Why, Mr. Jack Burden,
how are you, sir?


00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:48.293
You know, people would think
parish treasurer paid well enough...


00:09:48.464 --> 00:09:51.558
...a man wouldn't have to sell
household fix-it kits door-to-door.


00:09:51.734 --> 00:09:54.635
- People would think.
- Doesn't in Mason City.


00:09:54.804 --> 00:09:57.830
Well, I'm maybe not so good
at mathematics...


00:09:58.007 --> 00:10:00.202
...as some other parish treasurers
you may've met.


00:10:00.376 --> 00:10:02.503
Or too good at it.


00:10:03.145 --> 00:10:05.773
How much they steal
on the schoolhouse contract?


00:10:05.948 --> 00:10:07.643
Well, let's see...


00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.083
Jeffers come in $ 142,000.


00:10:11.253 --> 00:10:13.551
Moore, $ 175,000.


00:10:13.723 --> 00:10:17.853
That's $33,000 split six ways,
5500 per commissioner.


00:10:18.027 --> 00:10:22.225
They done it so plain and pretty, well,
you'd almost have to admire them.


00:10:22.398 --> 00:10:25.060
Just point out Jeffers
uses nigra laborers...


00:10:25.234 --> 00:10:28.101
...skilled men, you know?


00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:31.967
Next thing, it's, "Lookie here, nigras
making more money than you men.


00:10:32.141 --> 00:10:34.075
Pushing wheelbarrows,
hauling dirt."


00:10:35.044 --> 00:10:38.536
And that's it. "Goodbye, Mr. Jeffers
and your low bid.


00:10:38.714 --> 00:10:41.615
You go build your nigra schoolhouse
somewhere else."


00:10:41.784 --> 00:10:44.685
Not that you didn't try and get people
to see what was going on.


00:10:44.854 --> 00:10:49.291
Oh, I yelled so long and loud about
these old boys lining they pockets...


00:10:49.458 --> 00:10:51.756
...l'm lucky to have
any job in Mason City:


00:10:51.927 --> 00:10:54.020
Government, door-to-door,
or any other variety.


00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:56.027
I stood out there
on that street corner...


00:10:56.198 --> 00:10:58.189
...pencil in one hand,
paper in the other...


00:10:58.367 --> 00:11:00.358
...trying to show people
the numbers.


00:11:00.536 --> 00:11:03.232
But you stop people out there
in that hot sun...


00:11:03.405 --> 00:11:05.635
...try to show them arithmetic...


00:11:05.808 --> 00:11:07.969
...well, they can't see it so clear...


00:11:08.144 --> 00:11:11.511
...through the sweat pouring in they
own eyes from they own hard labor.


00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.513
Especially if you put nigras
in the equation.


00:11:14.683 --> 00:11:17.516
- Why, you're likely to get beat up.
- Likely?


00:11:17.686 --> 00:11:19.779
Once or twice.


00:11:20.623 --> 00:11:22.056
You gonna run again in November?


00:11:22.224 --> 00:11:27.059
No, I'm done. A lame duck. Lucy too.
They got her fired from teaching.


00:11:27.229 --> 00:11:31.063
And I don't care. I don't want to teach
there just so they can steal money.


00:11:31.233 --> 00:11:34.669
That's right. You're looking at your
own private two-person leper colony.


00:11:34.837 --> 00:11:36.464
Sipping pop.


00:11:37.072 --> 00:11:39.006
So, what are you gonna do, then?


00:11:39.175 --> 00:11:44.340
I don't know. String my pa a fence,
slop some pigs, milk some cows.


00:11:47.783 --> 00:11:51.947
I'm gonna keep the faith, Mr. Burden,
that's what I'm gonna do.


00:11:52.488 --> 00:11:56.754
I'm gonna keep the faith
in the people, because you know why?


00:11:58.561 --> 00:12:00.688
Time...


00:12:00.863 --> 00:12:04.230
...brings all things to light.


00:12:04.834 --> 00:12:07.234
I trust it's so.


00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.435
Joe.


00:12:42.605 --> 00:12:44.630
Did you get a photograph of him?


00:12:44.807 --> 00:12:46.297
Who?


00:12:49.545 --> 00:12:52.036
The next mayor of this town.


00:13:03.692 --> 00:13:06.217
You know what people are saying?


00:13:07.096 --> 00:13:09.690
People are saying
that God himself had a hand...


00:13:09.865 --> 00:13:12.857
...in this schoolhouse business.


00:13:13.035 --> 00:13:17.768
That God stepped in
on Willie Stark's side.


00:13:18.307 --> 00:13:22.801
Yes, sir. He does work
in mysterious ways sometimes.


00:13:22.978 --> 00:13:24.878
Sometimes...


00:13:25.047 --> 00:13:27.880
...he has somebody else do it.


00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:32.919
Sends over a fat man in a striped suit
with a big car to do his will.


00:13:33.088 --> 00:13:36.524
Well, I have had
some worse employers, I admit that.


00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.491
What you want?


00:13:39.929 --> 00:13:42.921
Well, I wanna work for you,
Mr. Stark.


00:13:43.098 --> 00:13:46.534
And you wanna work for the people,
unless I been misinformed.


00:13:46.702 --> 00:13:48.966
People vote me,
I'd be privileged to serve them.


00:13:49.138 --> 00:13:53.097
- What, as the county treasurer?
- Yes, sir.


00:13:54.677 --> 00:13:57.168
Mr. Stark, you could run
for mayor of Mason City...


00:13:57.346 --> 00:14:00.873
...and you could win without climbing
out of bed in the morning.


00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.779
You just put the word out...


00:14:03.218 --> 00:14:07.086
...about Willie Stark, who tried to take
on the crooks single-handed...


00:14:07.256 --> 00:14:09.588
...Willie Stark,
who tried to warn us...


00:14:09.758 --> 00:14:14.559
...Willie Stark, who could have saved
our kids if we'd have just listened.


00:14:15.464 --> 00:14:20.993
Now, I'm not talking about Willie Stark
for the mayor of Mason City. No, sir.


00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:23.661
I'm talking about Willie Stark...


00:14:23.839 --> 00:14:28.640
...as the next governor
of the great state of Louisiana.


00:14:30.312 --> 00:14:33.804
Now, you saw a man
holding out a handful of cash to you...


00:14:33.983 --> 00:14:35.883
...and you said no.


00:14:36.051 --> 00:14:37.643
This is what I see.


00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:40.288
I see a man in a booth...


00:14:40.456 --> 00:14:43.391
...looking down at a ballot,
a working man.


00:14:43.559 --> 00:14:48.690
And he sees three names there:
Harrison, MacMurphy and Stark.


00:14:49.098 --> 00:14:50.827
Now, what this man really sees...


00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.969
...is that picture in the newspaper
of them three little coffins...


00:14:54.403 --> 00:14:57.497
...and the one man since
the great Governor Stanton died...


00:14:57.673 --> 00:15:01.302
...that had the guts to buck the powers
that killed them.


00:15:02.611 --> 00:15:04.909
Now, that man, that voting man,
he's got a pencil...


00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.207
...he checks a box,
you wake up governor.


00:15:07.583 --> 00:15:10.177
And that little lady lying
beside you...


00:15:10.352 --> 00:15:14.652
...the one that don't favor liquor...


00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:17.991
...she wakes up the governor's wife.


00:15:23.132 --> 00:15:24.690
That's what I see.


00:15:26.168 --> 00:15:30.468
Now, why don't you take a minute
with your orange pop...


00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:34.238
...see if you can't see it too...


00:15:35.844 --> 00:15:37.539
...governor.


00:16:07.209 --> 00:16:09.040
You got your speech?


00:16:09.278 --> 00:16:11.007
All right.


00:16:14.583 --> 00:16:16.483
Willie Stark!


00:16:21.924 --> 00:16:23.824
Thank you, folks.


00:16:25.727 --> 00:16:27.285
Thank you kindly.


00:16:29.098 --> 00:16:31.464
My name's Willie Stark
from Mason City yonder...


00:16:32.901 --> 00:16:36.462
...and I'm pleased to have a chance
to talk with you all here today.


00:16:36.638 --> 00:16:38.606
Now, friends...


00:16:39.441 --> 00:16:43.172
...what I wanna talk about is
something that's been troubling me.


00:16:43.345 --> 00:16:46.143
- Coffee, please.
- Yes, ma'am.


00:16:50.486 --> 00:16:52.750
Can I sit with you?


00:16:52.921 --> 00:16:54.479
Or anything else.


00:16:55.824 --> 00:16:57.485
No, thanks.


00:16:58.127 --> 00:17:01.153
- You don't like my looks?
- I don't care about anybody's looks...


00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.321
...but I can't recall
ever going for anyone...


00:17:03.499 --> 00:17:06.024
...who reminds me
of a box of spilled spaghetti.


00:17:06.568 --> 00:17:09.731
Miss Burke, I'm sitting here
having a cup of coffee.


00:17:09.905 --> 00:17:12.203
I'm almost through,
then you couldn't sit with me...


00:17:12.374 --> 00:17:15.309
...which is what you asked for.
- Sorry.


00:17:18.213 --> 00:17:19.942
Not working
for Sen-Sen Puckett anymore.


00:17:20.516 --> 00:17:23.679
- Now, he wasn't a bad-looking fellow.
- Heel.


00:17:23.852 --> 00:17:26.082
Well, sure, politically and elsewise.


00:17:26.255 --> 00:17:28.086
Who didn't know that?


00:17:28.257 --> 00:17:30.487
I guess I'm slower on some things
than others.


00:17:30.659 --> 00:17:32.559
- Like you.
- Am I?


00:17:32.728 --> 00:17:34.855
- I think so.
- I think not.


00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.292
Not on this charade.


00:17:37.733 --> 00:17:40.361
That's the topic of the interview.


00:17:40.536 --> 00:17:43.266
Then tell me, if you're so smart.


00:17:43.438 --> 00:17:47.306
All right. Harrison's a city man,
MacMurphy's a cracker.


00:17:47.476 --> 00:17:50.274
Not a cracker precisely,
but enough of one to worry Harrison...


00:17:50.445 --> 00:17:51.810
...that crackers won't know
the difference.


00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:55.541
So Harrison looks for someone
to split the cracker vote.


00:17:55.717 --> 00:17:58.413
Hears about an honest man
up in Crackerville...


00:17:58.587 --> 00:18:01.055
...where some cracker kids go down
with a fire escape...


00:18:01.223 --> 00:18:04.090
...that was supposed to be stuck with
more than spit to their schoolhouse.


00:18:04.259 --> 00:18:06.887
Sends his man Tiny Duffy up there
to romance him...


00:18:07.062 --> 00:18:10.327
...and then Sadie Burke
to romance him some more.


00:18:10.499 --> 00:18:12.126
Both telling him how good he is...


00:18:12.301 --> 00:18:15.668
...how he has better than a chance
in hell to change things in this state...


00:18:15.837 --> 00:18:17.361
...where nothing will ever change.


00:18:17.539 --> 00:18:19.404
Because you and Tiny
and the rest of them...


00:18:19.575 --> 00:18:22.669
...don't care how much of a fool
you make a man.


00:18:22.844 --> 00:18:25.176
And you do care, I suppose?


00:18:25.347 --> 00:18:27.577
I didn't say that. I don't care.


00:18:27.749 --> 00:18:30.741
If I did, I'd do something about it,
wouldn't I?


00:18:30.919 --> 00:18:34.013
No, I'd rather watch from here.


00:18:35.224 --> 00:18:37.852
Like passing a car crash.


00:18:38.393 --> 00:18:41.328
I know you all can't see this
from all the way back there...


00:18:41.496 --> 00:18:44.226
...but I've got a pie chart
representing it.


00:18:44.566 --> 00:18:48.161
And you can see here where
public welfare and hospitals end up.


00:19:04.886 --> 00:19:08.652
They should be the same.


00:19:09.291 --> 00:19:12.260
Rather, the ratio...


00:19:30.312 --> 00:19:32.280
We should go.


00:19:33.482 --> 00:19:35.279
Not yet.


00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.509
Let's go in again.


00:19:51.199 --> 00:19:52.996
You don't wanna swim?


00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.511
How you think we doing?


00:20:15.424 --> 00:20:16.823
Fine, I guess.


00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:19.288
You think?


00:20:19.928 --> 00:20:22.396
That how you reporting it?


00:20:22.831 --> 00:20:24.128
Sure.


00:20:25.701 --> 00:20:30.604
Seems to me they listen less and less
the further I get from home.


00:20:30.772 --> 00:20:33.434
Well, that makes sense,
don't you think?


00:20:37.245 --> 00:20:38.940
Maybe...


00:20:40.449 --> 00:20:41.973
...you trying to say too much.


00:20:43.785 --> 00:20:45.685
I'm telling them
what they need to know:


00:20:45.854 --> 00:20:47.583
Taxes, wages, highways.


00:20:47.756 --> 00:20:49.553
Well, maybe it's how
you're telling them.


00:20:49.725 --> 00:20:52.523
Maybe if you told them
the way you tell Lucy or Tiny or me...


00:20:52.694 --> 00:20:54.855
...or anyone face to face,
they'd listen better.


00:20:55.364 --> 00:20:56.797
I don't know how that is.


00:20:56.965 --> 00:20:59.229
Hard to know how you sound
to somebody else.


00:20:59.401 --> 00:21:02.666
Mad, fed up, like you mean business
is how you sound.


00:21:02.838 --> 00:21:04.999
But not on the platform.
You climb three steps...


00:21:05.173 --> 00:21:09.269
...you sound like the rest of them. Like
a man who wants to win an election.


00:21:12.581 --> 00:21:14.515
Willie...


00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.208
Yeah?


00:21:18.286 --> 00:21:19.514
What?


00:21:23.692 --> 00:21:25.216
Nothing.


00:21:26.428 --> 00:21:30.125
Well, a man don't have to be governor.


00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.434
I don't deny wanting it.


00:21:33.602 --> 00:21:37.800
I won't lie to you,
I lie awake wanting it.


00:21:37.973 --> 00:21:42.637
But sometimes a man
can want something so bad...


00:21:43.011 --> 00:21:46.003
...be so full of want...


00:21:47.115 --> 00:21:51.449
...he plain forget what it is he want.


00:21:53.655 --> 00:21:56.351
I could have been a good governor.


00:21:56.591 --> 00:21:59.651
A lot better than them other fellas.


00:22:02.764 --> 00:22:05.597
But I ain't gonna be governor.


00:22:11.907 --> 00:22:13.135
Hi.


00:22:13.308 --> 00:22:15.299
Come on in. Why not?


00:22:16.144 --> 00:22:18.476
Oh, Mr. Stark.


00:22:20.515 --> 00:22:21.948
Sadie.


00:22:25.754 --> 00:22:27.051
What's up?


00:22:27.222 --> 00:22:30.089
Willie here was just telling me
how he's not gonna be governor.


00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:33.288
You told him?


00:22:36.832 --> 00:22:39.392
No, I didn't, as a matter of fact, no.


00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:43.597
Told me what?


00:22:48.944 --> 00:22:52.573
Told me what?


00:23:04.726 --> 00:23:07.786
Oh, yeah, well, that makes sense.


00:23:07.963 --> 00:23:10.056
I see.


00:23:13.702 --> 00:23:16.671
So that's true? I'm being used.


00:23:16.838 --> 00:23:19.136
So they tell me.


00:23:20.642 --> 00:23:24.840
I saw it in his eyes the first time
he come to see me, Tiny.


00:23:26.147 --> 00:23:29.344
But I just pushed it out of my head.


00:23:30.852 --> 00:23:33.412
Pushed it clean out.


00:23:37.092 --> 00:23:38.821
I should've known better.


00:24:03.585 --> 00:24:05.644
Mr. Stark?


00:24:06.154 --> 00:24:07.382
Mr. Stark?


00:24:17.766 --> 00:24:20.826
You thought you were the little
white lamb of God, didn't you?


00:24:21.970 --> 00:24:26.066
Just waiting for the chance to stand
on your hind legs and make a speech.


00:24:27.676 --> 00:24:31.237
They would have paid you
to play the part. They pay me.


00:24:31.513 --> 00:24:34.607
But you were too stupid
to see even that.


00:24:35.283 --> 00:24:37.478
You did it for free.


00:24:39.321 --> 00:24:44.190
You're just their dumb sacrificial sap
and I'm...


00:24:49.364 --> 00:24:51.924
I'm sorry I let them.


00:25:15.924 --> 00:25:19.121
Your stomachaches, your colics,
your bloats, your diarrhea.


00:25:33.108 --> 00:25:35.099
You're looking a little peaked.


00:25:36.611 --> 00:25:38.670
I can't imagine.


00:25:38.847 --> 00:25:40.474
Slept like a baby.


00:25:42.884 --> 00:25:44.146
Got your speech?


00:25:47.055 --> 00:25:49.421
All right, then. Let's go. It's time.


00:25:50.558 --> 00:25:52.822
"Hail, Hail, The Gang's All Here."


00:25:54.162 --> 00:25:55.527
What?


00:25:55.997 --> 00:25:57.931
The song.


00:25:59.567 --> 00:26:03.003
Yeah. That's what it is.


00:26:28.596 --> 00:26:30.621
Hello. Hello.


00:26:31.132 --> 00:26:32.997
How are you?


00:26:33.168 --> 00:26:36.137
Here's that speech
you was just asking about.


00:26:38.907 --> 00:26:43.310
My name is Willie Stark
from Mason City yonder.


00:26:44.446 --> 00:26:45.913
I had a speech...


00:26:46.314 --> 00:26:48.976
...about this state and what it needs.


00:26:49.851 --> 00:26:52.547
There's no use in me telling you
about it, you are the state.


00:26:52.721 --> 00:26:54.586
You know what you need.


00:26:54.756 --> 00:26:57.850
Look at the knees of your pants.


00:26:58.326 --> 00:27:00.487
Look at your crops.


00:27:00.662 --> 00:27:01.993
Look at your kids.


00:27:02.163 --> 00:27:05.155
You got holes and rot...


00:27:05.333 --> 00:27:08.496
...and ignorant offspring
on account of this state.


00:27:10.171 --> 00:27:13.868
Well, I had a speech,
but I ain't got it no more.


00:27:14.042 --> 00:27:17.569
Mr. Duffy got it now
in his fat little hands.


00:27:17.746 --> 00:27:18.974
Don't you, Tiny?


00:27:19.147 --> 00:27:22.514
Go ahead, show the people.
Hold it up.


00:27:24.219 --> 00:27:26.881
Well, since he got it...


00:27:27.055 --> 00:27:29.615
...l'm gonna have to say
something else.


00:27:30.225 --> 00:27:32.284
It's all right.


00:27:32.761 --> 00:27:35.787
Because I got something else
to say.


00:27:36.264 --> 00:27:40.564
I got a story about a redneck hick.


00:27:40.735 --> 00:27:43.135
He's like yourselves, if you please.


00:27:43.605 --> 00:27:49.009
Well, this fella, a while back,
this hick...


00:27:49.978 --> 00:27:53.414
...started thinking about
all the other hicks...


00:27:53.581 --> 00:27:55.947
...what he could do for them.


00:27:57.085 --> 00:27:59.053
Well, one day...


00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:04.157
...it came down
with the powerful force...


00:28:04.325 --> 00:28:06.953
...of God's own hand...


00:28:07.562 --> 00:28:12.090
...when the only brick schoolhouse
ever built in his parish...


00:28:12.267 --> 00:28:17.728
...collapsed on account of it was built
with politics-rotted brick.


00:28:17.906 --> 00:28:23.640
And it killed and mangled
a batch of poor, young scholars.


00:28:25.547 --> 00:28:28.038
Oh, you know this story.


00:28:28.216 --> 00:28:29.911
You heard it.


00:28:30.084 --> 00:28:32.484
He fought the politics
that built that schoolhouse...


00:28:32.654 --> 00:28:34.952
...with rotten brick and bolts.


00:28:36.457 --> 00:28:38.322
But he lost.


00:28:38.493 --> 00:28:40.256
He lost.


00:28:40.695 --> 00:28:42.629
And it fell.


00:28:43.131 --> 00:28:44.359
It fell.


00:28:46.801 --> 00:28:49.964
Well, it wasn't long...


00:28:50.138 --> 00:28:54.837
...before some public officials
from the city...


00:28:55.009 --> 00:28:57.978
...rode out in their big fine car...


00:28:58.146 --> 00:29:03.174
...and told this hick how they
wanted him to run for governor.


00:29:04.152 --> 00:29:06.518
Them in them striped pants,
they told me...


00:29:06.688 --> 00:29:09.521
...MacMurphy was a limberback...


00:29:09.691 --> 00:29:13.889
...Joe Harrison, he was just a tool
of the city machine.


00:29:14.062 --> 00:29:19.364
And they wanted this nobody,
do-gooder hick...


00:29:19.534 --> 00:29:21.661
...to step in,
give them some honest government.


00:29:21.836 --> 00:29:23.633
You know who they were?


00:29:24.706 --> 00:29:26.936
In that big fine car?


00:29:30.778 --> 00:29:34.874
They was Joe Harrison's
own lickspittles...


00:29:35.049 --> 00:29:38.416
...coming in to split MacMurphy's
hick vote!


00:29:38.586 --> 00:29:41.054
That's right! Your hick vote!


00:29:41.222 --> 00:29:43.156
There he is!


00:29:43.324 --> 00:29:44.586
There he is right there.


00:29:44.759 --> 00:29:50.493
There's the Judas Iscariot lickspittle
nose-wiper from the city, right there.


00:29:50.665 --> 00:29:54.328
Come on, Tiny. Look at him.
Joe Harrison's dummy.


00:29:54.502 --> 00:29:57.562
Come on, take a bow. Come on. No,
come on now, people wanna see you.


00:29:57.739 --> 00:30:00.731
Take a bow, come on.
There he goes.


00:30:01.442 --> 00:30:04.104
No! No, let him lie! Let him lie!


00:30:04.279 --> 00:30:07.407
Let that hog lie in his own filth!


00:30:07.582 --> 00:30:10.050
Let him lie,
but listen to me, you hicks.


00:30:10.218 --> 00:30:13.847
That's right, I'm not the only one here.
You hicks too.


00:30:14.022 --> 00:30:18.721
They fooled you, too, just like
they fooled me a thousand times.


00:30:18.893 --> 00:30:21.453
But it's time I fooled somebody.


00:30:21.629 --> 00:30:24.120
It's time I fooled them.


00:30:24.299 --> 00:30:28.099
Them big-city, striped-pants lickspittle
hick-haters.


00:30:28.269 --> 00:30:31.136
I'm running for governor on my own.


00:30:31.306 --> 00:30:35.640
I'm coming for them
and I'm coming for blood!


00:30:41.382 --> 00:30:43.577
First thing I'm gonna do
is build me a road out...


00:30:43.751 --> 00:30:47.619
...across the swamps and alligators
and anything else that gets in my way.


00:30:47.789 --> 00:30:50.690
A thousand miles of concrete,
if that's what it takes...


00:30:50.858 --> 00:30:54.726
...so I can come out here and visit with
my fellow hicks on a regular basis.


00:30:54.896 --> 00:30:57.956
Then I'm gonna build me a bridge
across that mighty Mississippi.


00:30:58.132 --> 00:31:00.930
Name it after myself
because I'm the one who built it.


00:31:01.102 --> 00:31:03.127
Then I'm gonna build you all
new schools.


00:31:03.304 --> 00:31:07.104
Send your kids home with free tablets
and pencils and books...


00:31:07.275 --> 00:31:11.177
...to study and learn on the way
to the new university I'm gonna build...


00:31:11.346 --> 00:31:13.974
...where every one of them can go.


00:31:14.148 --> 00:31:15.740
Same as rich folks' kids.


00:31:16.384 --> 00:31:19.979
Now, I hope you're listening,
you hicks.


00:31:20.154 --> 00:31:23.851
Because I don't wanna drive
all the way back home...


00:31:24.025 --> 00:31:27.825
...just to drive back out here
next week to tell you again.


00:31:27.996 --> 00:31:29.361
And this is it:


00:31:31.132 --> 00:31:33.600
If you don't vote...


00:31:33.768 --> 00:31:35.998
...you don't matter.
You don't matter!


00:31:36.170 --> 00:31:37.933
You don't matter!


00:31:38.106 --> 00:31:41.303
And then you're just as ignorant
as them in the city say you are...


00:31:41.476 --> 00:31:43.467
...while they stealing food
off your table...


00:31:43.644 --> 00:31:46.135
...and every nickel out your pocket,
saying, "Thank you."


00:31:46.314 --> 00:31:51.479
Because then you are just a bunch
of ignorant hicks who got nothing...


00:31:51.652 --> 00:31:53.643
...because you deserve nothing.


00:31:54.022 --> 00:31:55.785
So listen to me.


00:31:55.957 --> 00:31:57.549
Listen here.


00:31:57.725 --> 00:31:59.317
Lift your eyes...


00:31:59.494 --> 00:32:04.295
...and look on the God's blessed
and unflyblown truth:


00:32:04.465 --> 00:32:09.869
You are a hick and ain't nobody
never helped a hick but a hick hisself.


00:32:10.038 --> 00:32:15.032
It's up to you
to nail these parasites up.


00:32:15.209 --> 00:32:19.475
- Up to you and me and God.
- Amen!


00:32:19.647 --> 00:32:22.912
- Nail up Joe Harrison!
- Nail him up!


00:32:23.084 --> 00:32:25.780
- Nail up MacMurphy!
- Nail him up!


00:32:25.953 --> 00:32:29.184
And nail up any bastard
that gets between you...


00:32:29.357 --> 00:32:31.552
...and the roads and the bridges
and schools...


00:32:31.726 --> 00:32:33.216
...and the food you need.


00:32:33.394 --> 00:32:35.828
You give me the hammer
and I'll do it.


00:32:35.997 --> 00:32:38.557
I'll nail their hides to the barn door.


00:32:38.733 --> 00:32:40.564
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:40.735 --> 00:32:42.396
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:42.570 --> 00:32:44.265
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:44.439 --> 00:32:46.270
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:46.441 --> 00:32:48.170
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:48.342 --> 00:32:50.071
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:50.244 --> 00:32:52.007
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:52.180 --> 00:32:53.841
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:54.015 --> 00:32:55.744
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:55.917 --> 00:32:57.509
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:57.685 --> 00:32:59.516
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:32:59.687 --> 00:33:01.348
- Nail them up!
- Nail them up!


00:33:30.451 --> 00:33:32.578
More about Stark?


00:33:32.753 --> 00:33:34.846
He's colorful. Makes it easy.


00:33:35.022 --> 00:33:37.957
You know me,
always looking for easy.


00:33:49.837 --> 00:33:53.136
Jack. You know what
The Chronicle line is on the election.


00:33:53.474 --> 00:33:57.570
Sure. MacMurphy again because of his
brilliant record as an administrator...


00:33:57.745 --> 00:33:59.975
...and high integrity as a statesman.


00:34:00.148 --> 00:34:03.982
Why can't you put that in your column,
a little less of Stark's raving madness?


00:34:08.556 --> 00:34:11.252
Listen, Jack.
I know Stark's a friend of yours but...


00:34:11.425 --> 00:34:14.394
He's not a friend of mine. Personally,
I don't care who's governor.


00:34:14.562 --> 00:34:16.462
Are you telling me what to write,
or am I mistaken?


00:34:16.631 --> 00:34:19.464
- You know The Chronicle line.
- All right.


00:34:21.135 --> 00:34:23.933
What do you mean, "All right"?


00:34:28.543 --> 00:34:30.807
I mean it the way I said it.


00:34:42.356 --> 00:34:46.122
I, Willie Stark, do solemnly swear...


00:34:46.294 --> 00:34:50.697
...that I will support the constitution
and laws of the state of Louisiana.


00:34:50.865 --> 00:34:54.301
Willie didn't need me
to get himself elected.


00:34:54.468 --> 00:34:56.493
He won by a landslide.


00:34:57.138 --> 00:35:00.665
By the biggest margin in the history
of the state.


00:35:00.841 --> 00:35:05.039
- All the duties incumbent upon me
as governor so help me God.


00:35:05.846 --> 00:35:08.280
Which isn't to say
everyone voted for him.


00:35:08.449 --> 00:35:10.508
Jack, get up Mason City.


00:35:10.685 --> 00:35:12.277
My editor didn't vote for him.


00:35:12.453 --> 00:35:14.887
- Thinks he's Jesus Christ
come down off the cross...


00:35:16.457 --> 00:35:18.584
The publisher of this paper
didn't vote for him.


00:35:20.027 --> 00:35:23.360
These men didn't vote for him.


00:35:24.765 --> 00:35:26.494
Or these.


00:35:26.667 --> 00:35:29.636
The governor's education bill
does not pass.


00:35:29.804 --> 00:35:34.935
Or the old boys in the Senate who
were in the pockets of the oilmen.


00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:42.576
My mother didn't vote for him.


00:35:44.952 --> 00:35:47.648
This is my mother.


00:35:48.789 --> 00:35:51.087
She doesn't vote.


00:35:52.693 --> 00:35:57.392
Over there, on her dressing table...


00:35:57.565 --> 00:36:00.261
...that's her with her first husband.


00:36:00.434 --> 00:36:04.564
First of four, if I recollect.


00:36:04.739 --> 00:36:09.506
And that's my godfather on the right,
the best man.


00:36:09.677 --> 00:36:12.475
He didn't vote for Willie either.


00:36:13.180 --> 00:36:14.613
In fact...


00:36:14.782 --> 00:36:19.082
...I think it's safe to say nobody from
where I'm from voted for Willie Stark.


00:36:19.987 --> 00:36:22.455
And why should they?


00:36:22.623 --> 00:36:24.454
His promises to the poor...


00:36:24.625 --> 00:36:26.718
...to build roads and bridges
and schools...


00:36:27.194 --> 00:36:30.652
...were a declaration of war
on the rich.


00:36:33.234 --> 00:36:35.429
They wanted him out.


00:36:50.017 --> 00:36:51.348
You Jack Burden?


00:36:55.923 --> 00:36:58.687
I've come at the behest of the boss.


00:36:59.026 --> 00:37:00.323
Who?


00:37:00.494 --> 00:37:02.792
The boss? The governor?


00:37:11.238 --> 00:37:14.173
Governor, let me put it in simple words
so you understand:


00:37:14.342 --> 00:37:17.778
There's no money for all these things
you wanna do for the poor.


00:37:17.945 --> 00:37:19.537
Oh, there's money, senator.


00:37:19.714 --> 00:37:22.148
You're wrong there.
There's plenty of money.


00:37:22.416 --> 00:37:25.874
Every kilowatt comes out of the river,
every barrel of oil from the ground.


00:37:26.053 --> 00:37:28.544
But that doesn't belong to you, sir.


00:37:28.723 --> 00:37:32.523
That's right. Don't belong to you either
or them. Belongs to the state.


00:37:33.361 --> 00:37:37.798
How about the state don't tax just 5%
to build my roads, we take it all?


00:37:37.965 --> 00:37:41.059
These are some powerful companies
you talking about taking money from.


00:37:41.235 --> 00:37:43.635
- They ain't gonna stand for it.
- They ain't the power.


00:37:43.804 --> 00:37:45.795
The power's in the hands
of the powerless...


00:37:45.973 --> 00:37:47.998
...and those hands
have handed it to me.


00:37:54.215 --> 00:37:57.048
Realistically, they'll approve
half the money, maybe.


00:37:57.218 --> 00:37:58.879
And that's after we beat them up.


00:37:59.053 --> 00:38:01.283
So we build them half a highway.


00:38:01.455 --> 00:38:04.356
Mile of concrete, mile of dirt,
mile of concrete, mile of dirt...


00:38:04.525 --> 00:38:06.015
...all the way to Shreveport.


00:38:06.193 --> 00:38:08.661
Now, how's anybody gonna drive
on that?


00:38:08.829 --> 00:38:10.558
People ain't gonna stand for that.


00:38:10.731 --> 00:38:12.528
They like their roads finished.


00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:13.928
That's right.


00:38:14.802 --> 00:38:16.360
What's right?


00:38:16.704 --> 00:38:19.400
Hey, Jack. Sadie, take Tiny
out of here, explain it to him.


00:38:19.573 --> 00:38:21.905
- He just said it and he don't get it.
- Come on, Tiny.


00:38:22.076 --> 00:38:23.941
- You want something to eat?
- No, thank you.


00:38:24.111 --> 00:38:25.544
- Well, sit down.
- Hi, Sadie.


00:38:25.713 --> 00:38:27.044
Hey.


00:38:30.551 --> 00:38:31.950
I heard you got fired.


00:38:32.119 --> 00:38:34.679
Oh, you heard wrong. I quit.


00:38:34.855 --> 00:38:38.621
That's smart. When I get done with that
outfit, they won't be able to pay you...


00:38:38.793 --> 00:38:41.591
...nor the nigra
who sweeps the floor.


00:38:41.762 --> 00:38:44.492
- You want a job?
- Working for whom?


00:38:44.665 --> 00:38:47.691
- The state?
- Hell, no.


00:38:48.102 --> 00:38:49.399
Me.


00:38:49.570 --> 00:38:51.561
You, me, Sadie, Tiny.


00:38:51.739 --> 00:38:55.106
Tiny? I was surprised to hear
Tiny was back.


00:38:56.110 --> 00:38:58.806
Well, somebody gotta be
lieutenant governor.


00:38:59.079 --> 00:39:01.047
Yeah, sure.


00:39:03.417 --> 00:39:05.749
I keep Tiny around...


00:39:05.953 --> 00:39:09.411
...to remind me of something
I never wanna forget.


00:39:10.157 --> 00:39:11.886
And that is?


00:39:12.359 --> 00:39:17.023
When they come around
sweet-talking, don't listen.


00:39:17.565 --> 00:39:19.192
Never again.


00:39:22.536 --> 00:39:25.528
What would I be doing for you?


00:39:28.509 --> 00:39:30.602
Sweet-talking.


00:39:37.551 --> 00:39:39.610
All right, everybody.


00:39:39.787 --> 00:39:41.482
What on earth is that?


00:39:41.655 --> 00:39:43.919
- This is a ballista.
- A what?


00:39:44.091 --> 00:39:47.925
Jack will tell you all about it.
Jack, come on. Tell them.


00:39:48.095 --> 00:39:52.156
It's a pre-gunpowder weapon
fired with the tension of animal sinew.


00:39:52.333 --> 00:39:53.891
Oh, my God.


00:40:08.315 --> 00:40:09.543
Jack?


00:40:11.785 --> 00:40:15.221
Right. See the eagle
on top of the clock?


00:40:17.024 --> 00:40:18.514
One...


00:40:19.493 --> 00:40:20.721
...two...


00:40:35.309 --> 00:40:38.107
They say you're in politics,
Mr. Burden?


00:40:38.279 --> 00:40:40.679
It must be fascinating
to be in politics.


00:40:41.248 --> 00:40:44.513
It's not, I assure you.


00:40:44.685 --> 00:40:47.210
Well, they say
you're very influential.


00:40:47.388 --> 00:40:50.414
It must be fascinating
to be very influential.


00:40:50.591 --> 00:40:51.888
I honestly wouldn't know.


00:40:52.059 --> 00:40:56.792
Don't let him kid you, Miss DuMonde.
My godson Jack is very influential.


00:40:56.964 --> 00:40:58.864
Like when he was a newspaperman.


00:40:59.033 --> 00:41:00.728
All right, then, yes, I'm influential.


00:41:00.901 --> 00:41:04.064
Any pals in the pen anyone
wants pardoned, I'll put in the word.


00:41:04.238 --> 00:41:06.672
Well, there is gonna be
somebody in the pen.


00:41:06.840 --> 00:41:09.502
Before it's over,
what's going on there?


00:41:09.677 --> 00:41:11.668
All these wild goings-on.


00:41:12.780 --> 00:41:16.876
Fella giving away the state.
Free this, free that, free the other.


00:41:17.051 --> 00:41:20.953
Every wool-hat jackass
thinking the world is free.


00:41:21.355 --> 00:41:23.448
Who's gonna pay?
That's what I wanna know.


00:41:24.124 --> 00:41:25.716
Who's he think's gonna pay?


00:41:25.893 --> 00:41:28.453
Standard Oil and the utility companies,
I imagine.


00:41:28.629 --> 00:41:31.097
And anyone else that can afford
to pay their share.


00:41:31.265 --> 00:41:33.460
You and me, George. We'll pay.


00:41:33.634 --> 00:41:35.465
Government's committed
these days...


00:41:35.636 --> 00:41:39.333
...giving services
we never heard of back when.


00:41:39.506 --> 00:41:43.875
And he's gonna tax this state to death.
Drive business right out.


00:41:44.044 --> 00:41:46.103
You don't think it boils down to this:


00:41:46.280 --> 00:41:48.339
If the government,
for quite a long time now...


00:41:48.515 --> 00:41:50.278
...had done anything
for the people...


00:41:50.451 --> 00:41:53.284
...they wouldn't have got fed up
and elected Mr. Stark.


00:41:54.254 --> 00:41:58.054
Well, you ask him this
next time you see him:


00:41:58.225 --> 00:42:02.594
Ask him how much grabbing there is,
all that money flowing.


00:42:03.631 --> 00:42:06.828
Then you ask him what's he gonna do
when they impeach him.


00:42:07.601 --> 00:42:10.001
There's a constitution in this state...


00:42:10.170 --> 00:42:13.435
...or was, before he blew it to hell.


00:42:14.308 --> 00:42:17.744
- I'll be sure to ask him.
- You do that.


00:42:17.911 --> 00:42:21.347
Jack, Miss DuMonde plays the piano.


00:42:22.149 --> 00:42:23.946
That's nice.


00:42:28.155 --> 00:42:32.251
You weren't like yourself today, son,
like you used to be.


00:42:32.426 --> 00:42:36.522
Mother, if I'm ever like I used to be,
do me a favor and shoot me.


00:42:39.166 --> 00:42:40.599
Who was that at lunch anyway?


00:42:40.768 --> 00:42:43.066
Mr. Peyton.
You've known him all your life.


00:42:43.237 --> 00:42:45.671
He builds electrical plants
or some such.


00:42:45.839 --> 00:42:47.739
The girl, Mother. Miss DuMonde.


00:42:47.908 --> 00:42:52.902
That's Mr. Orton's sister's child
and she will inherit his money.


00:42:53.080 --> 00:42:55.981
Somebody ought to wait
until she inherits it, then marry her...


00:42:56.150 --> 00:42:58.846
...and drown her in her bathtub.


00:42:59.586 --> 00:43:02.612
Oh, don't worry,
I'd like to drown her but I won't.


00:43:03.657 --> 00:43:05.989
Was Mr. Peyton saying
those people you're with...


00:43:06.160 --> 00:43:09.061
...are mixed up in some sort of graft?


00:43:09.229 --> 00:43:11.390
Graft's what you call it
when who's doing it...


00:43:11.565 --> 00:43:14.500
...doesn't know which fork to use.
- Well, whatever you call it.


00:43:14.668 --> 00:43:16.795
- Because I worry to think that...
- I don't know.


00:43:16.970 --> 00:43:20.030
How would I, careful as I am not
to know what anybody anywhere...


00:43:20.240 --> 00:43:22.299
...is doing at any time?


00:43:36.490 --> 00:43:37.889
Oh, Jack, make a note.


00:43:38.058 --> 00:43:40.822
Find out where they got
Senator Tucson's boy locked up.


00:43:40.994 --> 00:43:44.327
- What's his name?
- The boy? Hell, I don't remember.


00:43:44.498 --> 00:43:46.932
Find out when's the trial,
get a lawyer down there.


00:43:48.502 --> 00:43:51.630
- Who? Evans?
- Not Evans.


00:43:51.805 --> 00:43:54.035
Find somebody
with less oil in his hair...


00:43:54.208 --> 00:43:56.039
...and don't look like he sing
with a band.


00:43:56.210 --> 00:43:58.576
Put one of your pals on it.


00:43:59.580 --> 00:44:01.377
You have any idea who it was got cut?


00:44:01.548 --> 00:44:05.416
I don't care if it was the sainted aunt
of the Apostle Paul.


00:44:05.586 --> 00:44:07.747
Well, I just happen to know.


00:44:07.921 --> 00:44:10.151
Fella's son of a doctor, paper said.


00:44:10.324 --> 00:44:13.521
They're pretty important around here,
you know, a doctor in the country.


00:44:13.694 --> 00:44:16.128
They think they're somebody.


00:44:16.296 --> 00:44:19.322
And maybe it gets out you're
trying to fix it to get the boy off.


00:44:19.500 --> 00:44:21.434
Wouldn't do you any good.


00:44:21.835 --> 00:44:24.895
- Now, it appears to me, maybe...
- You don't know a goddamn thing.


00:44:25.672 --> 00:44:27.401
Had you been listening...


00:44:27.574 --> 00:44:30.202
...I told Jack to prime
the lawyer through a pal.


00:44:30.377 --> 00:44:33.141
Find somebody who don't need to
see his name in lights.


00:44:33.313 --> 00:44:36.441
That way, nobody knows
who picked him wasn't me.


00:44:37.484 --> 00:44:41.750
Might as well been the pope
himself far as anybody knows.


00:44:42.322 --> 00:44:43.584
All right.


00:44:44.625 --> 00:44:46.252
I get you.


00:44:46.426 --> 00:44:48.417
Yeah, just barely.


00:45:06.113 --> 00:45:08.013
- Hey, there, Pop.
- How you doing, son?


00:45:08.682 --> 00:45:12.209
- How you making out?
- Oh, I'm getting along.


00:45:12.386 --> 00:45:14.752
Good to see you.
You looking good.


00:45:16.156 --> 00:45:19.956
- I brought the infantry here.
- How are you?


00:45:20.127 --> 00:45:23.062
- More prettier than ever.
- Hey, Grandpa.


00:45:23.397 --> 00:45:24.989
How you doing, buddy?
How's the arm?


00:45:25.165 --> 00:45:27.998
- He gonna be all-American.
- I know he is. I know he is.


00:45:30.237 --> 00:45:35.573
All right, governor, sir, here we go.
One, two...


00:46:01.568 --> 00:46:03.092
Bastard.


00:46:08.408 --> 00:46:10.103
Give me a slug.


00:46:13.547 --> 00:46:16.038
Pa don't favor drinking.


00:46:16.216 --> 00:46:18.741
Used to be Lucy didn't favor it.


00:46:21.088 --> 00:46:24.421
I don't know what she do
or don't favor no more.


00:46:24.758 --> 00:46:26.726
Not that it matters.


00:46:30.097 --> 00:46:34.864
Yeah, I must have poured 10,000
gallons of swill in them troughs.


00:46:35.769 --> 00:46:38.567
Still doing it. Pouring swill.


00:46:38.739 --> 00:46:41.139
Some things never change.


00:46:45.345 --> 00:46:46.334
Hey.


00:46:49.249 --> 00:46:51.843
- What's up?
- Judge Irwin.


00:46:54.354 --> 00:46:55.981
Judge Irwin what?


00:46:56.924 --> 00:46:59.188
- Spill it.
- I'll spill it when I have my breath.


00:46:59.359 --> 00:47:01.657
You're using it up
explaining you don't have it.


00:47:01.828 --> 00:47:04.456
You think it's funny?
You won't when I tell you.


00:47:04.765 --> 00:47:07.563
- You tell me later.
- Byram rang up.


00:47:08.201 --> 00:47:10.795
He said the afternoon papers
have got the judge saying...


00:47:10.971 --> 00:47:14.304
...the allegations warrant
a full-on investigation.


00:47:15.208 --> 00:47:16.436
Two-timing bastard.


00:47:18.011 --> 00:47:20.479
That two-timing bastard.


00:47:22.649 --> 00:47:23.877
Clear them out.


00:47:24.051 --> 00:47:25.985
Tiny was figuring
on having supper up here.


00:47:26.153 --> 00:47:27.882
Clear them all out.


00:47:45.572 --> 00:47:47.005
Which way up there?


00:47:48.976 --> 00:47:51.843
Jack, tell Sugar
how to get to the house.


00:47:52.846 --> 00:47:55.440
It's your people live down here.


00:48:12.265 --> 00:48:13.755
Suppose he don't open up?


00:48:15.602 --> 00:48:18.093
Make him. What I pay you for?


00:48:30.450 --> 00:48:33.681
- Yeah, who is it?
- It's Jack.


00:48:35.355 --> 00:48:36.982
Jack?


00:48:37.157 --> 00:48:38.488
Well, I'll be.


00:48:39.159 --> 00:48:40.990
Hey, come on in.


00:48:43.263 --> 00:48:44.992
You're not in any trouble, are you?


00:48:46.700 --> 00:48:48.964
No, Jack's not in any trouble.


00:48:49.136 --> 00:48:52.367
Matter of fact, he doing all right,
all things considered.


00:48:58.011 --> 00:49:01.811
I trust you don't mind
if Jack pours me a slug.


00:49:02.182 --> 00:49:04.616
I didn't know his duties
ran to those of manservant...


00:49:04.785 --> 00:49:07.219
...but if I'm mistaken, I'm sorry.
- Oh, hell.


00:49:07.387 --> 00:49:10.447
Sometimes Jack pours me a drink,
sometimes I pour him one.


00:49:10.624 --> 00:49:13.184
Sometimes I pour myself one.


00:49:13.693 --> 00:49:15.354
I could pour you one.


00:49:15.529 --> 00:49:17.224
No, thank you.


00:49:22.135 --> 00:49:23.796
This today's?


00:49:23.970 --> 00:49:27.201
Yeah, I don't get much time
to read the papers...


00:49:27.374 --> 00:49:30.172
...rushing around the state
doing the good work.


00:49:30.544 --> 00:49:33.172
Well, perhaps, I can relieve
your curiosity on one point.


00:49:33.346 --> 00:49:35.337
Somewhere in there's my opinion
on the severity...


00:49:35.515 --> 00:49:38.040
...of the allegations against you,
if that's of interest.


00:49:38.218 --> 00:49:40.345
Somebody told me that.


00:49:41.021 --> 00:49:43.990
But you know how rumor
hath a thousand tongues.


00:49:44.157 --> 00:49:47.786
And how them newspaper boys,
they can exaggerate some.


00:49:48.228 --> 00:49:49.855
It's no exaggeration.


00:49:50.997 --> 00:49:52.658
Yeah, I see.


00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:55.991
If you're clear on that
and finished with your drink...


00:49:56.169 --> 00:49:58.103
...l'd appreciate it
if you'd just get out.


00:49:58.271 --> 00:50:01.206
Hey, thank you, judge,
I think I will have just one more spot.


00:50:04.077 --> 00:50:07.535
So I see it there in the paper,
and I hear you say it...


00:50:07.714 --> 00:50:10.649
...but are you sure
you took it to the Lord in prayer?


00:50:11.351 --> 00:50:13.216
I settled it in my mind.


00:50:13.386 --> 00:50:16.844
See, that's unsettling.


00:50:17.023 --> 00:50:19.491
Because if I recollect right,
I recollect that...


00:50:19.659 --> 00:50:22.059
...when we had our conversation
in town that time...


00:50:22.229 --> 00:50:25.790
...you sort of felt like what MacMurphy
and his boys were saying about me...


00:50:26.066 --> 00:50:27.328
...was beneath contempt.


00:50:27.501 --> 00:50:30.299
I made no commitment to you
or to them, only to my conscience.


00:50:30.470 --> 00:50:33.496
- I beg your pardon, your what?
- I beg yours.


00:50:37.711 --> 00:50:41.078
You been toiling around politics too
long to use a word like conscience...


00:50:41.248 --> 00:50:42.772
...so easily.


00:50:42.949 --> 00:50:46.783
No, my change of conscience came
when certain features of your...


00:50:47.154 --> 00:50:49.952
...public services, shall we say,
came to my attention.


00:50:50.123 --> 00:50:53.024
Somebody dug something up for you?
In the dirt?


00:50:53.193 --> 00:50:56.128
Yeah, not just one thing
and not very deep.


00:50:56.696 --> 00:50:57.924
Well, dirt's a funny thing.


00:50:58.098 --> 00:51:02.728
Ain't nothing but dirt on God's green
earth except what's under the water.


00:51:02.903 --> 00:51:05.736
And that's dirt too,
come to think of it.


00:51:06.306 --> 00:51:07.967
Dirt makes the grass green...


00:51:08.508 --> 00:51:10.066
...let it breathe.


00:51:10.243 --> 00:51:14.270
The diamond on my wife's finger
ain't nothing but dirt got awful hot.


00:51:14.447 --> 00:51:17.416
What are we, but dirt blowed off
the hands of God almighty?


00:51:17.584 --> 00:51:20.610
You and me
and George Washington.


00:51:22.522 --> 00:51:23.955
And Jack there.


00:51:26.960 --> 00:51:28.257
Still doesn't alter the fact.


00:51:28.428 --> 00:51:32.296
I'm not trying to alter anything,
just illuminate it.


00:51:33.833 --> 00:51:35.061
Yeah.


00:51:35.235 --> 00:51:38.602
You saying MacMurphy and his bunch,
yelling for my impeachment...


00:51:38.772 --> 00:51:41.570
...they're responsible,
law-abiding men?


00:51:41.841 --> 00:51:45.106
Yeah, they're responsible all right,
to Alta Power and oil companies...


00:51:45.278 --> 00:51:46.745
...and the rest of them thieves.


00:51:46.913 --> 00:51:48.141
I wouldn't know about that.


00:51:48.315 --> 00:51:52.081
Only way to not know
is to not wanna know.


00:51:53.853 --> 00:51:57.584
I'm retired, Mr. Stark. A reporter
asked my opinion and I gave it.


00:51:57.757 --> 00:52:00.988
If you was retired, no reporter
would wanna ask you anything.


00:52:02.095 --> 00:52:04.222
What you say matters.


00:52:04.531 --> 00:52:07.193
A lot more than you pretend it don't.


00:52:09.035 --> 00:52:11.026
So I'm asking you...


00:52:11.938 --> 00:52:13.872
...call off the dogs.


00:52:14.975 --> 00:52:19.844
Asking is different than telling
and that sounded like telling to me.


00:52:20.580 --> 00:52:22.605
Didn't it to you, Jack?


00:52:26.987 --> 00:52:29.285
You been a judge a long time.


00:52:29.456 --> 00:52:31.083
Yes, I have.


00:52:33.159 --> 00:52:35.627
How would it feel, do you think...


00:52:36.863 --> 00:52:39.388
...to not be one no more?


00:52:42.669 --> 00:52:45.934
No man has ever been able
to intimidate me.


00:52:46.106 --> 00:52:49.906
I said what I said and I see no reason
to say or think anything different.


00:52:50.710 --> 00:52:54.612
Despite your expositions
on laws and men, sir.


00:52:57.217 --> 00:52:58.445
Suit yourself.


00:52:59.719 --> 00:53:03.450
You're right, Jack.
He don't scare easy.


00:53:05.825 --> 00:53:11.092
Judge, it's more in pain
than wrath I go.


00:53:11.665 --> 00:53:14.828
Let's go.
It's past Sugar Boy's bedtime.


00:53:16.002 --> 00:53:17.970
Your employer is calling you, Jack.


00:53:18.805 --> 00:53:21.774
I wouldn't go around
advertising this visit to anyone.


00:53:21.941 --> 00:53:23.738
In case you change your mind.


00:53:34.220 --> 00:53:35.949
Bastard.


00:53:36.856 --> 00:53:40.451
Well, Jackie,
you got a job cut out for you.


00:53:41.061 --> 00:53:44.497
- MacMurphy.
- No, the judge.


00:53:45.965 --> 00:53:47.933
You bring down the lion...


00:53:48.101 --> 00:53:51.969
...the rest of the jungle will quake
in fear and they'll all fall into line.


00:53:52.572 --> 00:53:55.803
- I won't find anything.
- Oh, yes, you will.


00:53:56.009 --> 00:54:00.673
A man is conceived in sin
and born in corruption...


00:54:00.847 --> 00:54:04.305
...and passeth from the stink of
the didie to the stench of the shroud.


00:54:06.386 --> 00:54:08.251
You'll find something.


00:54:09.089 --> 00:54:10.647
And make it stick.


00:54:19.265 --> 00:54:22.996
Apart from pleasing the boss,
I could see little advantage...


00:54:23.169 --> 00:54:28.835
...in finding anything beyond what
was already known about Judge Irwin.


00:54:31.611 --> 00:54:34.774
What was known
was that he was kind to you...


00:54:34.948 --> 00:54:38.679
...when your father left you
and your mother without saying why.


00:54:41.187 --> 00:54:43.052
What was known
was that he taught you...


00:54:43.223 --> 00:54:45.691
...the things your father
should have:


00:54:46.760 --> 00:54:48.887
How to be a gentleman.


00:54:49.095 --> 00:54:51.689
How to firmly shake a hand.


00:54:52.198 --> 00:54:55.895
How to safely load a shotgun
and lead a duck if you wanted to hit it.


00:54:59.706 --> 00:55:01.640
What was known...


00:55:02.142 --> 00:55:06.010
...was that he was more of a father
to you than your real father...


00:55:08.181 --> 00:55:10.615
...who you didn't know at all.


00:56:36.569 --> 00:56:38.537
Hold it, please.


00:56:39.072 --> 00:56:41.336
Governor's penthouse.


00:56:46.246 --> 00:56:49.306
How you doing digging
something up on Judge Irwin?


00:56:49.682 --> 00:56:51.172
Nothing.


00:56:51.384 --> 00:56:53.614
Nothing. Found nothing
or done nothing?


00:56:53.786 --> 00:56:57.813
There was nothing to find. I could
dig to China, wouldn't find anything.


00:56:57.991 --> 00:56:59.822
- And I'm not framing him.
- Framing?


00:56:59.993 --> 00:57:02.018
Ain't nobody talking about framing.


00:57:02.195 --> 00:57:03.560
That's never necessary.


00:57:03.730 --> 00:57:06.722
The truth is always sufficient.
You just find the truth.


00:57:07.133 --> 00:57:08.657
It's a waste of time and money.


00:57:08.835 --> 00:57:11.303
Jesus, doesn't anybody listen
to what I say anymore?


00:57:11.471 --> 00:57:15.032
You don't wanna do it, don't do it.
Or are you just looking for a raise?


00:57:15.742 --> 00:57:18.643
I'm gonna give you $ 100 raise
whether you want it or not.


00:57:18.811 --> 00:57:20.403
If I wanted more money, I'd make it.


00:57:22.382 --> 00:57:24.407
You gonna tell me
you work for me for love?


00:57:24.584 --> 00:57:27.485
I don't know why I work for you,
but it ain't for love or money.


00:57:27.654 --> 00:57:29.053
Well, that's right, it's not.


00:57:29.956 --> 00:57:32.186
And you don't know why.


00:57:34.193 --> 00:57:35.592
But I do.


00:57:36.996 --> 00:57:38.395
Why?


00:57:38.731 --> 00:57:43.532
Boy, you work for me
because I'm the way I am...


00:57:43.703 --> 00:57:46.069
...and you the way you are...


00:57:46.239 --> 00:57:50.198
...and that's just an arrangement
founded in the natural order of things.


00:57:58.017 --> 00:58:00.383
She sure could skate.


00:58:04.057 --> 00:58:05.786
Right now...


00:58:06.326 --> 00:58:08.590
...hidden away in chambers...


00:58:09.062 --> 00:58:12.190
...not out here in the open
like you and me...


00:58:13.366 --> 00:58:16.767
...there's a legislature
full of hyena-headed...


00:58:16.936 --> 00:58:20.372
...belly-dragging sons of bitches...


00:58:20.607 --> 00:58:24.236
...setting around trying to figure out
how to impeach me.


00:58:25.778 --> 00:58:28.941
Now, they say it's because
I got crooks on the payroll.


00:58:29.115 --> 00:58:30.980
I say, "Is that all?"


00:58:32.085 --> 00:58:35.054
Of course I got them.
I got a can of oil in the garage too...


00:58:35.221 --> 00:58:36.984
...because there ain't a machine
made by man...


00:58:37.156 --> 00:58:41.559
...don't need a squirt of that
from time to time just to keep running!


00:58:44.330 --> 00:58:46.560
But my crooks...


00:58:47.767 --> 00:58:49.962
...unlike theirs...


00:58:50.136 --> 00:58:53.037
...are all atremble...


00:58:53.272 --> 00:58:55.638
...to be too crooked.


00:58:56.509 --> 00:59:00.240
They're itty-bitty compared
to their crooks in there.


00:59:00.413 --> 00:59:02.881
The Standard Oil
and the power companies.


00:59:03.049 --> 00:59:05.244
Besides, I got my eye on mine.


00:59:05.418 --> 00:59:08.046
Ain't nobody watching
over these crooks.


00:59:08.655 --> 00:59:11.681
Ain't nobody got their eye on them...


00:59:11.858 --> 00:59:16.227
...while they rob
the resources of this state!


00:59:17.664 --> 00:59:20.462
Who made that son of a bitch
what he is? Who made him governor?


00:59:20.633 --> 00:59:23.067
And he goes and two-times me?
I'll kill him.


00:59:23.536 --> 00:59:26.232
No, he's two-timing Lucy.


00:59:26.406 --> 00:59:29.603
You need some other kind of
arithmetic for what he's doing to you.


00:59:29.776 --> 00:59:32.836
Lucy, she's a fool. She's...


00:59:33.813 --> 00:59:36.373
- I don't know what.
- His wife.


00:59:37.517 --> 00:59:41.385
A hick with a college degree
from some Baptist hole in the ground.


00:59:43.856 --> 00:59:45.653
What was she like?


00:59:46.626 --> 00:59:49.686
- I didn't know Lucy any further back...
- The slut on skates.


00:59:50.997 --> 00:59:53.329
I don't know,
I was looking at her skates.


00:59:53.499 --> 00:59:55.490
Sure you were.


00:59:57.870 --> 01:00:01.033
- Was she pretty?
- Look, just forget it.


01:00:02.475 --> 01:00:04.375
How young was she?


01:00:05.278 --> 01:00:08.042
- Who cares?
- Look at me.


01:00:23.229 --> 01:00:27.529
He'll be back.
The world is full of sluts on skates.


01:00:29.368 --> 01:00:33.771
Skates, grass skirts, geisha outfits.


01:00:39.545 --> 01:00:41.570
Contortionists.


01:00:44.817 --> 01:00:49.083
Every man a king
Every man a king


01:00:49.255 --> 01:00:53.419
For you can be a millionaire


01:00:53.593 --> 01:00:57.586
But there's something
Belonging to others


01:00:57.764 --> 01:01:01.564
Well, there's enough
For all people to share


01:01:02.001 --> 01:01:06.370
When it's sunny June
Or December too


01:01:06.539 --> 01:01:09.940
In the wintertime or spring


01:01:10.610 --> 01:01:12.703
Well, there'll be peace without end


01:01:12.879 --> 01:01:15.211
Every neighbor a friend


01:01:15.381 --> 01:01:19.044
With every man a king


01:01:26.259 --> 01:01:29.751
The judge married money.
Savannah money.


01:01:29.929 --> 01:01:32.557
The daughter of an industrialist
out there.


01:01:32.732 --> 01:01:34.700
He's clean, Willie.
He's washed in the blood.


01:01:37.103 --> 01:01:40.664
- You call yourself a detective.
- I'm most certainly not...


01:01:40.840 --> 01:01:43.604
The son of a bitch
is washed in whitewash!


01:01:43.776 --> 01:01:45.437
- Wanting it isn't the same as being it.
- I know!


01:01:45.611 --> 01:01:48.102
- I can feel it.
- That isn't the same either.


01:01:48.281 --> 01:01:50.146
Where did you find this itty-bitty out?


01:01:50.316 --> 01:01:52.181
Hall of Records. It's all there.


01:01:52.351 --> 01:01:54.649
Marriage licenses,
property deeds, public record.


01:01:54.821 --> 01:01:58.587
The public record is for the public,
not us. That's why it's called that.


01:01:58.758 --> 01:02:00.487
You ain't gonna find nothing there!


01:02:01.427 --> 01:02:03.987
Now, I told you to dig,
not scuff your shoe a little bit.

